I4M2YzZTU1M2U1NWEwOGZjMDk2YzNhNTNjY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/soulcodex/agentic/commit/35aec988196082558e42c91c06f33b188ba18628","sha":"35aec988196082558e42c91c06f33b188ba18628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/soulcodex/agentic/commits/35aec988196082558e42c91c06f33b188ba18628"}],"sha":"eda8cec6d46f283f3e553e55a08fc096c3a53ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/soulcodex/agentic/commits/eda8cec6d46f283f3e553e55a08fc096c3a53ccd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47703157?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/soulcodex","id":47703157,"login":"soulcodex","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAzMTU3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/soulcodex","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/soulcodex/agentic/commits/35aec988196082558e42c91c06f33b188ba18628/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-04T10:20:30Z","email":"47703157+soulcodex@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roberto Garcia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-04T10:20:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: library profiles, write-plan skill, --link mode, drop opencode.json (#34)\n\n* fix(vendors): stop generating opencode.json — let users manage their own config\n\nopencode.json sets model, permissions, and MCP config — personal choices\nthat belong to the developer, not the library. Generating it caused more\nfriction than value. OpenCode still receives AGENTS.md natively and skills\nvia .opencode/skills/ symlink. T42 updated to assert the file is absent.\n\n* feat(profiles): add go-library profile\n\nAdds a composition profile for Go reusable packages intended to be\nimported by other modules. Focuses on API stability, backward compat,\nand minimal transitive dependencies rather than runtime service concerns.\nNo architecture or observability fragments — library has no ports or DI\nentrypoint. Skills lean toward documentation, changelog, and refactoring.\n\n* feat(profiles): add typescript-library profile\n\nAdds a composition profile for TypeScript packages published to npm or\na private registry. Focuses on strict typing, ESM-first output,\ntree-shakability, and semver discipline. No runtime framework or\narchitecture fragments. Skills lean toward documentation, changelog,\nand refactoring.\n\n* feat(skills): add write-plan skill for automatic plan persistence\n\nIntroduces an agent-invoked (not user-invoked) skill that silently writes\nevery plan to .agentic/plans/ at the end of any planning session. Primary\npurpose: prevent PLAN.md from being accidentally committed to any repo.\nComplements the existing persist-plan skill (user-triggered) without\nreplacing it. Includes plan-template.md as a resource file.\n\n* feat(tooling): add --link symlink deploy mode with sync-links command\n\nAdds opt-in --link flag to compose, deploy-skills, and vendor-gen that\nreplaces file copies with symlinks into the library root. Keeps the target\nrepo clean — only config.yaml, profile.yaml, and project-skills are\ncommitted; fragments, skills, and vendor-files are symlinked and gitignored.\n\nNew sync-links.sh script re-creates broken symlinks from agentic_root\nstored in .agentic/config.yaml. New justfile recipes: compose-linked,\ndeploy-linked, sync-links. POSIX-only — exits with a clear error on\nnon-POSIX systems. Default copy mode is fully unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"226a4cab26aa5301261c050a3c0078713b6069c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/soulcodex/agentic/git/trees/226a4cab26aa5301261c050a3c0078713b6069c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/soulcodex/agentic/git/commits/35aec988196082558e42c91c06f33b188ba18628","verification":{"payload":"tree 226a4cab26aa5301261c050a3c0078713b6069c2\nparent 897fab751ec2f3c4858563ae01aeab6a33229e9d\nauthor Roberto Garcia <47703157+soulcodex@users.noreply.github.com> 1775298030 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775298030 +0200\n\nfeat: library profiles, write-plan skill, --link mode, drop opencode.json (#34)\n\n* fix(vendors): stop generating opencode.json — let users manage their own config\n\nopencode.json sets model, permissions, and MCP config — personal choices\nthat belong to the developer, not the library. Generating it caused more\nfriction than value. OpenCode still receives AGENTS.md natively and skills\nvia .opencode/skills/ symlink. T42 updated to assert the file is absent.\n\n* feat(profiles): add go-library profile\n\nAdds a composition profile for Go reusable packages intended to be\nimported by other modules. Focuses on API stability, backward compat,\nand minimal transitive dependencies rather than runtime service concerns.\nNo architecture or observability fragments — library has no ports or DI\nentrypoint. Skills lean toward documentation, changelog, and refactoring.\n\n* feat(profiles): add typescript-library profile\n\nAdds a composition profile for TypeScript packages published to npm or\na private registry. Focuses on strict typing, ESM-first output,\ntree-shakability, and semver discipline. No runtime framework or\narchitecture fragments. Skills lean toward documentation, changelog,\nand refactoring.\n\n* feat(skills): add write-plan skill for automatic plan persistence\n\nIntroduces an agent-invoked (not user-invoked) skill that silently writes\nevery plan to .agentic/plans/ at the end of any planning session. Primary\npurpose: prevent PLAN.md from being accidentally committed to any repo.\nComplements the existing persist-plan skill (user-triggered) without\nreplacing it. Includes plan-template.md as a resource file.\n\n* feat(tooling): add --link symlink deploy mode with sync-links command\n\nAdds opt-in --link flag to compose, deploy-skills, and vendor-gen that\nreplaces file copies with symlinks into the library root. Keeps the target\nrepo clean — only config.yaml, profile.yaml, and project-skills are\ncommitted; fragments, skills, and vendor-files are symlinked and gitignored.\n\nNew sync-links.sh script re-creates broken symlinks from agentic_root\nstored in .agentic/config.yaml. New justfile recipes: compose-linked,\ndeploy-linked, sync-links. POSIX-only — exits with a clear error on\nnon-POSIX systems. Default copy mode is fully unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp0OXuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAenYQAJg5Idfl9PgeQXkhRWsKBPLD\nLDdzjuIKdIQmMyhgvwt5c4os2Uyw4JmKBZgV9jk/3K2ucwZjIX8SoC9quTyduK0x\n4SJ5gc0ef33pahBaiDwZmAI1feITwCsapMuvU2VOYgJOOtDexCkSXyya+IUZwUa2\nkLTu6aez3sQWEH2nz2Q9AdnR22b6BXVeDwdktB0pOFB39a1X8pKQm39iSjpHS174\nZJQjfKvIGbO0RMT+FIb6lD0wmzckYomsTQ5pE9SQqoyHbZF6PyMYSezr8dy3g8nt\nSCHFOgzTsvX2UTFvQeXGH5U+x/cP62brZsmFNBP09ucf7L8oxjAJnm4v1Lhpql60\nH4/SXrfIBzzzYwjC3ThdU9AUmtBBk+Ep+IpgVA6b9qm3B1NJwkMJY1ZdmMB69Gjn\nRhS1F1svA3EFHDF1CE3Pc6egrhrRH8zBp2rF9F9zdDnp7hXxybXoagj69ZosFOCK\nEHwqzFtyp9hqc+e5lAZHOaCCifCE6X7IztKgzHVlRrHHZ5O7O085XvbbTSIx2rMl\njjp9UP9cycaxrGQ0MFXRm0NkwEblzqbtJB/PI3SgJ6wFVwZJtARCicFSyj+LqI4h\nTgIO2CpUZc9lfvJQgTUJDIUMCc5drP50Kujhnn/jJ2Nwgse8KeLV17d+IsKjz/U2\n5NIZBbDV9A5SPPq7tCIT\n=keym\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-04T10:20:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users