com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-phase-orchestrator/commits/b9740d416fdea962ab2b26a846a8fda6da87d4bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T11:11:05Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T11:13:55Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(ci): repair the ten tests that the kernel-serving changes broke\n\nThe first hosted run of 6ac35673 failed ten tests in every Python job.\n\n- The Julia UPDE adapters imported juliacall.JuliaError before each call,\n  so four adapter tests raised ModuleNotFoundError where juliacall is not\n  installed. The exception type is now resolved only after a call fails.\n- runtime.cli.serve had no API autodoc entry; the runtime page documents\n  it, and the documentation inventory counts 99 API pages.\n- The container tests still expected ENV PYTHONPATH and a --help default\n  command. They now check the installed-package image and that the\n  default serve command names a shipped spec and options the CLI accepts.\n- The FFI workflow test now separates the whole-suite pytest runs, which\n  must exclude slow tests, from the native-runtime runs on named files.\n- The UPDE dispatch test''s stub backend returns wrapped phases, as the\n  output validator has required since 58707d41.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b52b","tree":{"sha":"e1530859889e2fde9