github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-phase-orchestrator/commits/9063c2aacc5b3d027a3b90a9103575ebc1a4fc0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:28:40Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:28:40Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(ssgf): draw fresh Langevin noise per call and refuse non-finite inputs\n\nWith the Rust kernel and no generator, add_langevin_noise passed the\nfixed seed 42, adding identical \"noise\" on every step while the NumPy\npath drew new noise; NaN temperature or step returned NaN silently. In\nboltzmann_weight a NaN energy or temperature made the NumPy path clamp\nto +700 and return the largest weight while Rust returned NaN. Inputs\nmust now be finite and the Rust path receives a fresh seed per call.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: ae6d","tree":{"sha":"5859bd06f52655ed0b8a07591ef568bf0cb6b220","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-phase-orchestrator/git/trees/5859bd06f52655ed0b8a07591ef568bf0cb6b220"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-phase-orchestrator/git/commits/9063c2aacc5b3d027a3b90a9103575ebc1a4fc0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"l