um/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-phase-orchestrator/commits/522486fd62e4fc3e9577819223cbf44a48abd218/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T20:56:18Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T20:56:18Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(cli): make queuewaves check analyse Prometheus data, not random noise\n\nspo queuewaves check, documented as a one-shot scrape-and-analyse health\ncheck for CI or cron, never contacted Prometheus: it fed seeded random\nnoise to every service and printed \"No anomalies detected.\" with exit\n0 even when the configured Prometheus did not exist. It now fetches\neach service''s recent history with one PromQL range query\n(PrometheusCollector.backfill) and exits 2, never \"healthy\", when a\nservice returns too little data. Docs describe exit codes 0/1/2; tests\nexercise the real HTTP path against a local Prometheus-format server.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: ae6d","tree":{"sha":"929053a137a236de7a3aa5aa64ad3ae6bdf30c41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-phase-orchestrator/git/trees/929053a137a236de7a3aa5aa64ad3ae6bdf30c41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-phase-orchestrator/git/commits/522486fd62e4fc3e9577819223cbf44a48abd218","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.g